      "problem": "Find the cofactor of ${g}_{42}$ in \n$G=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{5} & 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "First, to get the minor of ${g}_{42}$, we remove the $4$th row and $2$nd column: \n\n$$\nG=[\\begin{aligned}8 & ∗ & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & ∗ & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ ∗ & \\sqrt{5} & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ 11 & ∗ & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{42}=|\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 11 & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNow, the cofactor of ${g}_{42}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{42} & =(-1)^{4+2}{M}_{42} \\\\  & ={M}_{42} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 11 & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
